{
    "about": "Every display string renamed so that no word of a name is a word the player types, or a typo of one (AGENTS.md, \"A name evokes what it is\"). Ids are unchanged. Apply `phrases`, `lowercase` and `caseVariants` case-sensitively as whole phrases (never inside a longer word), longest first, in ONE pass so no replacement fires on another's output; a name with an apostrophe also appears escaped (\\') in single-quoted TypeScript. `shortForms` are the words prose shortens a renamed body to, applied only where the sentence means that body. `generatorWords` are replaced ONLY inside the named list, one for one, so every seeded draw is unchanged. Do not apply this to text that quotes the owner verbatim, or to the history kept on purpose in docs/world/writing/place-names.md, src/data/cultivation/place-names.ts (placeIdSlug and placeSeedKey key on the retired names), src/web/names-as-they-are-spelled.ts and the two name tests. \"spirit boat\" is the owner's genre word and was kept (the guard exempts \"boat\").",
